From: Phil Taylor <phil@m0vse.uk>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi-scripts: restore regular hostapd's mbssid config key

The regular OpenWrt hostapd parser accepts mbssid, not multiple_bssid.
Keep the existing netifd/UCI option name and MBSSID behavior; only fix the
generated hostapd key. The independent qca-wifi-6 vendor script/parser uses
multiple_bssid and is deliberately unchanged. The qca-wifi-7 feed is also
unchanged. This fixes all families selecting the regular wifi-scripts package.

--- a/package/network/config/wifi-scripts/Makefile
+++ b/package/network/config/wifi-scripts/Makefile
@@ -10,5 +10,5 @@
 PKG_NAME:=wifi-scripts
 PKG_VERSION:=1.0
-PKG_RELEASE:=1
+PKG_RELEASE:=2
 PKG_LICENSE:=GPL-2.0
 
--- a/package/network/config/wifi-scripts/files/lib/netifd/wireless/mac80211.sh
+++ b/package/network/config/wifi-scripts/files/lib/netifd/wireless/mac80211.sh
@@ -529,7 +529,7 @@
 ${channel_list:+chanlist=$channel_list}
 ${hostapd_noscan:+noscan=1}
 ${tx_burst:+tx_queue_data2_burst=$tx_burst}
-${multiple_bssid:+multiple_bssid=$multiple_bssid}
+${multiple_bssid:+mbssid=$multiple_bssid}
 #num_global_macaddr=$num_global_macaddr
 #macaddr_base=$macaddr_base
 $base_cfg
